SAGA driver test @N@ - for PrismRTG 1.3 beta 8
=============================================

A native PrismRTG driver for SAGA video, the Apollo V4 boards' and the
Apollo A6000's, so PrismRTG drives it directly instead of through
vampiregfx.card.

New in test 3:
  - the board is found the way Apollo's own driver finds it, by the board
    number SAGA reports: every V4 board (Firebird, Icedrake, Standalone,
    Manticore) and the A6000. Vampire V2 boards are not supported; the
    driver says so.
  - more screen sizes: 1920x1080, 1280x1024, 1280x800, 1440x900, 640x200
    and 720x405, up to 1920x1080 in all.
  - screen updates wait for SAGA's vertical blank (falling back to the
    system's if SAGA's line counter does not move).
  - 15-bit colour, and 8 MB of fast RAM for the screens (16 MB if 8 is not
    there in one piece).

It has NOT run on Apollo hardware yet: it is written from the Apollo
team's own description of the SAGA registers (thank you, flype and the
Apollo team). Expect the first try to need fixing. Nothing here changes
your current setup until step 2, and step 2 is easy to undo.

Needs: an Apollo V4 board or an Apollo A6000, and PrismRTG 1.3 beta 8
installed. If it says "no supported board", please post what ShowConfig
lists and the first lines PrismTest printed, so the board can be added.

In this drawer
  PrismTest            shows a test pattern with a driver, no PrismD
  Drivers/SAGA.driver  the driver


Step 1 - a test pattern (nothing installed, nothing changed)
-------------------------------------------------------------
PrismTest must run without PrismD, so start the Amiga with PrismRTG
skipped: hold the LEFT mouse button from power-on until Workbench is
up. Then open a Shell, CD into this drawer and run, one at a time:

  PrismTest BOARD=SAGA DEPTH=8
  PrismTest BOARD=SAGA DEPTH=16 WIDTH=800 HEIGHT=600
  PrismTest BOARD=SAGA DEPTH=24 WIDTH=800 HEIGHT=600
  PrismTest BOARD=SAGA DEPTH=32 WIDTH=1280 HEIGHT=720
  PrismTest BOARD=SAGA DEPTH=16 WIDTH=1920 HEIGHT=1080

Each shows a pattern for 10 seconds and then gives the display back:
colour bars across the top, a grey ramp, a checkerboard. Ctrl-C ends it
early. Wrong colours mean a wrong pixel format, a slanted picture a
wrong row length. Please note for each one what you saw (a photo is
perfect) and copy the Shell output - its first line names your board.


Step 2 - Workbench on it (only if step 1 looked right)
-------------------------------------------------------
  Copy Drivers/SAGA.driver LIBS:Prism/
  Copy ENVARC:Prism.prefs ENVARC:Prism.prefs.p96

Then edit ENVARC:Prism.prefs (Ed ENVARC:Prism.prefs): change the line
BOARD=P96 to BOARD=SAGA, and add a line LOG=SYNC. Save and reboot.

SAGA has fixed screen sizes: 640x200, 640x400, 640x480, 640x512,
720x405, 720x576, 800x600, 848x480, 960x540, 1024x768, 1280x720,
1280x800, 1280x1024, 1440x900, 1920x1080 and the small ones. If Workbench
was on a size SAGA does not have, it comes up on the native screen: pick
a PRISM: mode in Prefs/ScreenMode then.

Things worth trying: windows, a Shell, Amelinium, the pointer (the
hardware pointer is 16x16 - its colours and its position over the
screen), another screen dragged down (with Drag screens on), and
whether moving windows looks smooth or tears.


Getting back
------------
If there is no picture, or anything goes wrong: reboot holding the LEFT
mouse button (PrismRTG is skipped), then in a Shell

  Copy ENVARC:Prism.prefs.p96 ENVARC:Prism.prefs

and reboot - you are back on the P96 driver as before.


Please send
